LED behaviour: clear status indication on the three front LEDs (openwrt-one).

The board has three status LEDs — warm-white (pwm0/pin13), green (pwm1/pin15) and
amber (gpio/pin9, mislabelled "red" upstream). Stock config left them mostly dark:
white ran a barely-visible dim pattern (<0 500 25 500>), green/amber had no trigger.

New scheme (warm-white = powered/running, green = alive heartbeat, amber = attention):
- white: default-on  -> solid whenever Linux is up (the power/run light).
- green: heartbeat    -> pulses while running ("alive & healthy"); led-upgrade alias
  makes it blink fast during sysupgrade (white stays solid).
- amber: relabelled from RED to AMBER (matches the schematic); led-failsafe alias.
Drop led-boot / led-running aliases — the default-on / heartbeat triggers cover the
run state directly, without diag.sh forcing them solid. The amber "OTA pending /
recovery" slow-blink is driven separately (backend / u-boot env).
LAN LEDs (pin34/35) unchanged.

